; dsv4-validate-band.bml -- the physical validation window of the DeepSeek-V4 driver is WRITTEN AND PINNED, NOT RUN: its plan on the real IQ2XXS header, the dry door's output, every abort rule and the governor's ask
; on scripted readings, the holders on scripted process rows, the references' arithmetic, the receipt row, and what the driver cannot run yet. Nothing is opened, mapped or leased; no device is touched.
;
; WHAT THIS PINS. form-stdlib/bml/dsv4-validate.bml holds the window's definitions and observe/dsv4-validate-run.bml is the door. This band reads the IQ2XXS file's first 8,388,608 bytes (never a weight), builds the
; plan from it, runs the door once in its {"dry":1} mode (a nested read-only process: it reads the header window and the machine and prints; it opens nothing, takes no lease and writes no row), and exercises the rules
; on scripted vm readings (the governor's own reading shape) and scripted process rows (the walk's own row shape).
;
; AFTER REVIEW (2026-10-03): the window is never the default (empty stdin, {} and {"dry":1} each print the plan: the door is run all three ways in claim 2, and claim 4 reads dvr-go?; only {"go":1} runs it); the head
; is among the gaps the door can name; the wirespan probe is judged by its own limit (claim 8, on a scripted delta of a whole stack); the stream stage's estimate is the expert cache; a logits leg without its ids is
; a named waits row; and {"go":1} on a header with gaps maps nothing, writes the receipt row and releases the lease (claim 256).
; AFTER DRIVER STAGE 4 (2026-10-03): the gap list is the layout's (dsv4-layout.fk dvl-driver-gaps, one table of the types each role may carry) and reads EMPTY on the IQ2XXS header (its Q8_0 dense and output tensors
; and Q2_K down stacks are run), on reap25 and on both fixtures; the refusal path and the gap lines are exercised on a doctored fixture (claims 64 and 256); the ordering of ds4's own Q8_0 and Q2_K lanes is a
; note the plan prints (dvr-notes), never a gap.
; AFTER THE PROMPT IDS (2026-10-03): the logits leg no longer waits by default. The row beside the recording (tests/oracles/ds4-logits-capital-of-france-prompt.json, derived from the IQ2XXS header by
; bml/dsv4-chat-template.bml and held to the derivation by tests/ds4-recorded-references-band.bml) pins its 14 chat-templated prompt ids; the door reads them after a check (dvr-chat-ids-ok?) and a request's
; own logits_prompt_ids replace them. The dry plan prints the ids and the leg's ask; the leg waits only when neither a request nor the row holds (claim 1024).
; AFTER THE FIRST WINDOW (2026-10-03 06:47:57 WITA): the window stopped itself at the state stage on wired +198,148,096 B against a price of 18,270,208 B that was right (layout bit 512, open bit 512 and lease bit 256
; hold it to first principles and to the device's own ledger): the machine's wired memory is every process's and moves by hundreds of MB on this Mac by itself. The door names the organs of ours resident by process
; and judges nothing by a subtracted number (claim 2048).
; AFTER WINDOW 2 (2026-10-03 07:29:28 to 07:30:04 WITA): compile, map (own device bytes +86,284,566,528: the 80 GiB mapping), state, wirespan ('between') and layers 0 to 15 passed on the real file, and the run ended at
; layer 16 on ask-denied:compressor with the numbers that denied thrown away; 13 s later the compressor read 6.3 GiB against a cap of 32. Field 8 of host_vm_stat is vm_statistics64.compressor_page_count, the pages the
; compressor OCCUPIES ('Pages occupied by compressor'); the pages it STORES ('Pages stored in compressor') are not among host_vm_stat's 17 words, and vm_stat says them (dvr-stored-pages). The denial is a reading carried
; whole (the receipt's denied row and every stage line) and a denial for reserve or compressor is waited out with the governor's naps (claim 4096). Layers are no longer staged by this door (a sync and a machine reading
; a layer is a probe protocol, not the token path): the token door (observe/dsv4-token-run.bml) reads the token as it runs; the layer prices, the bytes of the tensors a layer's dispatches can touch, are its expected
; curve (claim 8192).
;
; Verdict 16383 when every claim lands:
;   1     the plan from the header: lease shared 26,787,475,292 B (dense 7,290,857,308 + 64 experts a layer 19,478,347,776 + KV at 64 positions 18,270,208) and 8 GiB private; the stages' asks (compile and map bounds
;         536,870,912 and 538,496,268 (the scratch plan holds the NaN scan's four bytes since the scan's count buffer is made at the open), the state 18,270,208, the wirespan slice 2,162,688 B of a 553,648,128 B stack, the head 562,774,036, the arena 19,478,347,776 at the default 64 slots, the logits' and the stream's expert cache 19,478,347,776): eight stages, none a layer (arena_slots 0, the whole-stack control, has seven: no arena stage)
;   2     the dry door: run as {"dry":1} it prints the plan (the lease, every stage, the layer prices, the organs of ours, the back-off, the abort rules, the references with the pinned SHA-256, the logits leg on its 14 pinned
;         prompt ids with its ask, the receipt path, the budget) and ends 'DRY ends: 8 stages would run', exits 0, and leaves no receipt row and no lease file behind
;   4     the abort rules on scripted readings, in their documented order: a reading under half the reserve reads host-memory-low; wired growth past the lease reads wired-above-lease; 20 minutes reads budget, 19 do not;
;         an unreadable machine reads memory-unreadable; low is named before the others; a quiet reading is ''; a stage's growth over twice its price is told (dvr-over-price?) and is no abort of its own
;   8     the ask and the wirespan: the governor denies a stage whose estimate crosses the wired cap (wired-cap) or the reserve, grants one that fits, and the lease asked for (derived working set + 8 GiB) is granted on a
;         scripted empty 128 GiB machine where the file's own size is denied; the wirespan probe reads 'slice' for a delta near the slice, 'stack' for half the stack or more, 'between' otherwise
;   16    the holders and the start check: a walk door, a learning lane, a ds4 process and another copy of this door each hold the GPU; this process's lineage and an unrelated process do not; the window may start only
;         with no holder, no other lease, a readable machine that is not low
;   32    the references' arithmetic: Pearson r (1 for identical, -1 for opposite, a hand value for a small pair), the top-k order and overlap, the agreement record, the tie budget over their top 64, the stream
;         matched count (24 for the recorded stream, the first index of a flip); the recorded logits file is the pinned one (1,588,387 B, SHA-256 3898af17...) and reads 129,280 values with the argmax 2581 at 36.7579117
;   64    the receipt row and the gaps: a scripted record writes one JSON line that parses, carries the schema, status, reason, lease, stages, wirespan, stream and logits fields; the driver's gaps read from the IQ2XXS
;         header, the reap25 header and the fixture are NONE (and the IQ2XXS plan carries the ordering note, the reap25 plan none); a doctored fixture (a Q8_0 projection retyped F16, the Q8_0 output retyped F16, one
;         Q2_K stack retyped MXFP8, one router retyped F32) reads four gap lines, the head's first; the receipt's logits row carries finite
;   128   the checks can fail and the band touches nothing: the boundary readings a rule must tell apart do tell apart (just under and just over each limit), a row that omitted the abort reason is not valid JSON
;         of the shape the receipt needs, and the window itself (dvr-window) is never called here: this file defines no call to it
;   256   the go path with gaps and the steps: dvr-refuse-gaps on the doctored header (with a 2 MiB lease this process took first) writes one receipt row (refused, driver-gaps, the 4 gaps), maps nothing and gives the
;         lease back; dvr-steps lists 9 steps with or without the logits ids (8 for the whole-stack control), and a logits leg that waits (a row that fails its check, claim 1024) is a named waits row in the log with no estimate
;   512   the stream records OUR margins (the stream leg runs on the raw prompt ids alone; the reference's tie budget is the logits leg's, which runs on the 14 pinned prompt ids): dvr-step reads, from hand-made
;         logits, our argmax, our top-two margin (0 on a tie) and the recorded id's gap below our top (-1 reads no id); the recorded id of step i is dvr-want-at (11111 at 0, 455 at 23, none at 24); the
;         receipt row carries stream_margins and stream_recorded_gap whole (24 values each). Plants: a record whose margins were not recorded reads an empty array; the gap read against the wrong recorded
;         id, and a margin read off the second place instead of the top, read different numbers
;   1024  the logits leg's default prompt ids: the pinned row reads [0 3476 477 260 11502 22896 128803 671 6102 294 8760 344 128804 128821] (BOS, system, User, the raw prompt of the stream leg,
;         Assistant, <think>), 14 of them, and the door takes them when the request supplies none (dvr-logits-from: pinned) and the request's own ids when it does (supplied); the nested door prints them
;         with the stage's ask (18.1 GiB), and prints a supplied list in their place. Plants on the row's shape, each read as no ids (the leg would wait): a wrong id, a wrong count (13), a missing BOS (the ids short of
;         it, and a BOS that is no id though the ids agree with their parts), the system dropped (9 ids that agree with their parts), a prompt that is not the stream's raw prompt, a prompt_tokens that is not
;         the recording's 14; the control row reads its 14
;   2048  THE ORGANS OF OURS ARE NAMED, NOT SUBTRACTED. The first window's own numbers (the state stage: price 18,270,208, wired +198,148,096) are told as over twice their price in the stage line and end nothing (the guard is the
;         lease: wired above it past the baseline); the compile stage (+309,854,208 on 536,870,912) is not over; scripted process rows read as organs [pid, resident, command], largest first, with this process left out and a
;         row with no resident bytes left out; the line names how many, how much they hold and the largest by name ('and N more' past six); what moved between two readings is every organ whose resident bytes changed by
;         64 MiB or more (a new organ by what it holds, a gone one by what it held), largest change first; the live organs read on this Mac are a list of [pid, resident, command] with this process not among them; the
;         stage line carries the machine's reading, the paging counters and the organs; the receipt row carries organs, moved, denied, vm_window and every stage's own_delta and vm; the nested dry door prints the organs
;         line; dvr-stage-run runs on a stage that does no work (its row carries six values: own device bytes 0 while Metal is not up, and the machine's reading), a stage that answers nothing reads stage-refused
;   4096  THE DENIAL AND THE WAIT (window 2). A scripted reading with the compressor at 40 GiB reads 'compressor' and dvr-denied-json carries reason, available, wired, compressor (40 GiB), its cap (32 GiB), the pages
;         stored (1,824,749), the need, the time waited and the asks, as a row that parses; the ask line names the compressor occupied against its cap; vm_stat's text reads stored 1,824,749 and occupied 413,974
;         pages and a missing name -1, and on this Mac host_vm_stat field 8 equals vm_stat's occupied count (within the seconds between the readings) while the stored count is the larger; the paging counters since the
;         window began read [available, wired, compressor, pageins, pageouts, swapins, swapouts] from two scripted readings and say so in the stage line. The wait, on a scripted sense, sleep and clock: three busy readings
;         then a quiet one grant after naps of 10, 20 and 40 s (70 s waited, 4 asks); wired-cap and an unreadable machine never sleep; a reserve denial waits; a denial that never lifts ends after naps of 10, 20, 40, 60, 60,
;         60, 60 s (310 s: the wait is 5 minutes, and a nap that would pass it is the last), and a wait with no bound (an hour) would nap over fifty times; an ask whose wait is 0 reads the first busy reading as the end; the
;         wait never passes the window's 20 minutes. The receipt carries denied and vm_window, and the nested dry door prints the back-off line
;   8192  THE LAYER PRICE IS THE BYTES ITS DISPATCHES CAN TOUCH (window 2: wired followed the weights and returned them): layer 0 is 3,018,191,320 B (dense 147,190,232 + the three whole stacks 1,811,939,328 + token_embd
;         1,059,061,760), layer 1 1,959,129,560 B (the smallest), layer 2 1,975,917,016 B, layer 42 1,972,815,320 B; the prices are never summed: the sum of all 43 (85,700,536,136 B) is over the 76.8 GiB wired cap on a
;         scripted empty 128 GiB machine (ask-denied:wired-cap) where the largest is granted; the dry plan names the largest, the smallest and the first and last (dvr-layers-line), and no stage of this door is a layer
;
; REQUIRES: host-local model files -- bits 1, 2, 32 and 64 read the IQ2XXS and reap25 model files' headers (host-local paths outside the tree; 8 MB windows) and the recorded logits are read through read_file_slice;
; bit 2 runs the door in a nested process three ways. No model is opened, no device is touched; claim 256 takes a 2 MiB governor lease and gives it back, and writes a scratch receipt it removes.
// preludes: form-stdlib/core.fk form-stdlib/line-grammar.fk form-stdlib/json.fk form-stdlib/dsv4-fixture-gguf.fk form-stdlib/bml/dsv4-validate.bml
section [form.bml] {
 class Dsv4ValidateBand {
  def dvb-bit(held, bit) = held ? bit : 0;
  def dvb-iq2() = "/Users/ursmuff/models/ds4-engine/gguf/DeepSeek-V4-Flash-IQ2XXS-w2Q2K-AProjQ8-SExpQ8-OutQ8-chat-v2-imatrix.gguf";
  def dvb-gib(n) = n * 1073741824;
  def dvb-mib(n) = n * 1048576;
  def dvb-pages(b) = b / 16384;
  def dvb-has?(s, part) = str_find(s, part, 0) >= 0;
  def dvb-near(a, b, tol) = (a - b) <= tol && (b - a) <= tol;
  // a reading in the governor's shape: [page, mem, free, active, inactive, wired, speculative, purgeable, compressor, pageins, pageouts, compressions, decompressions, swapins, swapouts, external, internal]
  def dvb-vm(mem, free, wired, comp) = [16384, dvb-gib(mem), dvb-pages(dvb-gib(free)), 0, 0, dvb-pages(dvb-gib(wired)), 0, 0, dvb-pages(dvb-gib(comp)), 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0];
  def dvb-quiet() = dvb-vm(128, 100, 10, 1);
  // a reading with the paging counters set (the governor's shape; indices 9 pageins, 10 pageouts, 13 swapins, 14 swapouts)
  def dvb-vm-counters(vm, pi, po, si, so) = append(append(vm[0:9], [pi, po]), append(vm[11:13], append([si, so], vm[15:17])));
  // a compressor occupying 40 GiB (over its cap of 32), a reserve short, a wired cap crossed, and the scripted clock a wait reads: [sense, sleep, now, say] over a state record
  def dvb-busy() = dvb-vm(128, 100, 10, 40);
  def dvb-short() = dvb-vm(128, 5, 10, 1);
  def dvb-capped() = dvb-vm(128, 100, 90, 1);
  def dvb-st() = record_new(0, "i", 0, "now", 0, "naps", [], "said", []);
  def dvb-sense-next(st, seq) { let i = record_get(st, "i"); let k = record_set(st, "i", i + 1); seq[i < len(seq) ? i : len(seq) - 1]; }
  def dvb-sleep(st, ms) { let a = record_set(st, "now", record_get(st, "now") + ms); let b = record_set(st, "naps", append(record_get(st, "naps"), [ms])); ms; }
  def dvb-say(st, s) = record_set(st, "said", append(record_get(st, "said"), [s]));
  def dvb-io(st, seq) = [() => dvb-sense-next(st, seq), ms => dvb-sleep(st, ms), () => record_get(st, "now"), s => dvb-say(st, s)];
  def dvb-g-busy(est) = dvr-wait-go(est, 0, dvb-io(dvb-st(), [dvb-busy()]), 10000, 0, 0);
  // organs as the door reads them: [pid, resident bytes, command], largest first; before and after for what moved
  def dvb-organs() = [[701, dvb-gib(49), "./fkwu observe/form-glass-live-run.fk"], [702, dvb-gib(3), "./fkwu observe/day-turn-run.bml"], [703, dvb-mib(100), "./fkwu x"]];
  def dvb-organs-before() = [[701, dvb-gib(5), "./fkwu observe/form-glass-live-run.fk"], [702, dvb-gib(3), "./fkwu observe/day-turn-run.bml"]];

  // ---- 1: the plan ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  def dvb-plan(m) {
   let opts = json-node-object([]);
   let stages = dvr-stages(m, opts);
   let layers = dvr-est-layers(m);
   let shared = dls-shared(m, 64, 64);
   let control = dvr-stages(m, parse-json("opts", "{\"arena_slots\":0}"));
   let said = print_str("  plan shared " ++ shared.str() ++ " stages " ++ [stages[0][1], stages[1][1], stages[2][1], stages[3][1], stages[4][1], stages[5][1], stages[6][1]].str() ++ " of " ++ len(stages).str() ++ " (control " ++ len(control).str() ++ ") layers " ++ layers[0].str() ++ " " ++ layers[42].str());
   shared == 26787475292 && dls-dense(m) == 7290857308 && dls-cache(m, 64) == 19478347776 && dvl-kv-total(m, 64) == 18270208 && mg-kv-margin() == dvb-gib(8)
    && stages[0][1] == 536870912 && stages[1][1] == 538496268 && stages[2][0] == "arena" && stages[2][1] == 19478347776 && stages[3][1] == 18270208 && stages[4][0] == "wirespan" && stages[4][1] == 2162688 && dvr-stack(m) == 553648128 && dvr-slice(m) == 2162688
    && stages[5][0] == "head" && stages[5][1] == 562774036 && stages[6][1] == 19478347776 && stages[7][1] == 19478347776 && stages[7][0] == "stream"
    && len(stages) == 8 && dvr-index-of(map(s => s[0], stages), "layers", 0) == 0 - 1 && dvr-arena-slots(opts) == 64
    && len(control) == 7 && control[2][0] == "state" && control[3][0] == "wirespan" && dvr-arena-slots(parse-json("opts", "{\"arena_slots\":0}")) == 0 && dvr-arena-slots(parse-json("opts", "{\"arena_slots\":24}")) == 24 && dvr-stages(m, parse-json("opts", "{\"arena_slots\":24}"))[2][1] == dls-cache(m, 24);
  }

  // ---- 2: the dry door, nested ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  def dvb-lease-names() = fs_list(mg-lease-dir()) ?? [];
  // the door run three ways: {"dry":1}, {} and an empty stdin: all three print the plan, take no lease and write no row
  def dvb-run-door(cmd) {
   let before = dvb-lease-names();
   let rowsBefore = file_size(dvr-receipt-path());
   let text = host-exec(cmd, "") ?? "";
   let rowsAfter = file_size(dvr-receipt-path());
   let after = dvb-lease-names();
   let said = print_str("  door [" ++ cmd ++ "]: " ++ len(text).str() ++ " bytes");
   rowsBefore == rowsAfter && len(before) == len(after) && dvb-plan-text-ok?(text);
  }
  def dvb-dry-door() = dvb-run-door("echo '{\"dry\":1}' | ./fkwu observe/dsv4-validate-run.bml 2>&1") && dvb-run-door("echo '{}' | ./fkwu observe/dsv4-validate-run.bml 2>&1") && dvb-run-door("./fkwu observe/dsv4-validate-run.bml </dev/null 2>&1");
  def dvb-plan-text-ok?(text) {
   dvb-has?(text, "[dsv4-validate] DRY: the plan below is what the window WILL do; nothing is opened, nothing mapped, no lease taken, no row written")
    && dvb-has?(text, "lease: shared 24.9 GiB (26787475292 B: dense 7290857308 + 64 experts a layer 19478347776 + KV at 64 positions 18270208), private 8.0 GiB, derived and not measured")
    && dvb-has?(text, "stage compile: ask 0.5 GiB (536870912 B)") && dvb-has?(text, "stage wirespan: ask 0.0 GiB (2162688 B)") && dvb-has?(text, "stage logits: ask 18.1 GiB (19478347776 B)")
    && dvb-has?(text, "stage arena: ask 18.1 GiB (19478347776 B); the slot arena: 64 experts a layer in buffers allocated once") && dvb-has?(text, "the routed expert stacks are NOT mapped")
    && dvb-has?(text, "layer prices (the token door's expected curve; no layer is staged here): 43 layers, each the bytes of the tensors its dispatches can touch, whole stacks included: the largest 3018191320 B (2.8 GiB, layer 0), the smallest 1959129560 B (layer 1), layer 0 with token_embd 3018191320 B, the last 1972815320 B")
    && dvb-has?(text, "[dsv4-validate] organs of ours resident: ") && !dvb-has?(text, "stage layers") && !dvb-has?(text, "together") && !dvb-has?(text, "ambient")
    && dvb-has?(text, "SHA-256 " ++ dvr-logits-sha()) && dvb-has?(text, "logits leg: will run on the 14 chat-templated prompt ids [0,3476,477,260,11502,22896,128803,671,6102,294,8760,344,128804,128821] pinned beside the recording (form/form-stdlib/tests/oracles/ds4-logits-capital-of-france-prompt.json")
    && dvb-has?(text, "a supplied logits_prompt_ids replaces them), ask 18.1 GiB (19478347776 B)") && !dvb-has?(text, "WAITS") && dvb-has?(text, "receipt: one dated row appended to receipts/dsv4-validation.jsonl")
    && dvb-has?(text, "abort on: a denied ask (reserve and compressor only after the wait above), host-memory-low, wired above the lease") && dvb-has?(text, "[dsv4-validate] back off: an ask denied for reserve or compressor (the machine is busy, not full) waits with the governor's naps (10 s doubling to 60 s), printing each reading, for at most 5 min an ask and never past the window's 20;")
    && dvb-has?(text, "a stage's wired growth against its price and the wirespan probe's kind (slice, between or stack) are read and recorded, not aborts") && dvb-has?(text, "the driver cannot run yet: nothing named by the header") && !dvb-has?(text, "type 8 (the driver reads")
    && dvb-has?(text, "stage stream: ask 18.1 GiB (19478347776 B)") && dvb-has?(text, "ordering: note, not a gap: the recorded stream was earned with ds4's own order") && !dvb-has?(text, "REFUSED")
    && dvb-has?(text, "[dsv4-validate] DRY ends: 8 stages would run") && !dvb-has?(text, "ABORT") && !dvb-has?(text, "REFUSED");
  }
  // the default is the plan: only {"go":1} (and no dry) is the window
  def dvb-go() {
   let none = json-node-object([]);
   let go = parse-json("opts", "{\"go\":1}");
   let both = parse-json("opts", "{\"go\":1,\"dry\":1}");
   let dry0 = parse-json("opts", "{\"dry\":0}");
   let goNo = parse-json("opts", "{\"go\":0}");
   dvr-dry?(none) && !dvr-go?(none) && !dvr-dry?(go) && dvr-go?(go) && dvr-dry?(both) && dvr-dry?(dry0) && dvr-dry?(goNo) && dvr-dry?(parse-json("opts", "{\"dry\":1}"));
  }

  // ---- 4: the abort rules ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  def dvb-rules() {
   let base = dvb-gib(4);
   let lease = dvb-gib(33);
   let quiet = dvb-vm(128, 100, 10, 1);
   let est = dvb-gib(1);
   let low = dvb-vm(128, 5, 10, 1);
   let high = dvb-vm(128, 100, 50, 1);
   let ok = dvr-abort-reason(quiet, base, lease, 60000) == "";
   let r1 = dvr-abort-reason(low, base, lease, 60000) == "host-memory-low" && dvr-abort-reason(dvb-vm(128, 100, 105, 1), base, lease, 0) == "host-memory-low" && dvr-abort-reason(dvb-vm(128, 100, 10, 60), base, lease, 0) == "host-memory-low";
   let r2 = dvr-abort-reason(high, base, lease, 60000) == "wired-above-lease" && dvr-abort-reason(dvb-vm(128, 100, 36, 1), base, lease, 0) == "" && dvr-abort-reason(dvb-vm(128, 100, 38, 1), base, lease, 0) == "wired-above-lease";
   let r3 = dvr-over-price?(2 * est + 1, est) && !dvr-over-price?(2 * est, est) && !dvr-over-price?(dvb-mib(128), 0) && dvr-over-price?(dvb-mib(129), 0) && dvr-abort-reason(quiet, base, lease, 0) == "";
   let r4 = dvr-abort-reason(quiet, base, lease, 1200001) == "budget" && dvr-abort-reason(quiet, base, lease, 1140000) == "" && dvr-abort-reason(quiet, base, lease, 1200000) == "";
   let r5 = dvr-abort-reason([], base, lease, 0) == "memory-unreadable" && dvr-abort-reason(dvb-vm(128, 5, 50, 1), base, lease, dvr-abort-ms() + 1) == "host-memory-low"
    && dvr-abort-reason(dvb-vm(128, 100, 50, 1), base, lease, dvr-abort-ms() + 1) == "wired-above-lease";
   let said = print_str("  rules " ++ [ok, r1, r2, r3, r4, r5].str());
   ok && r1 && r2 && r3 && r4 && r5 && dvr-abort-ms() == 1200000 && dvr-budget-ms() == 1800000 && dvb-go();
  }

  // ---- 8: the ask and the wirespan --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  def dvb-ask(m) {
   let empty = dvb-vm(128, 110, 4, 0);
   let shared = dls-shared(m, 64, 64);
   let derived = shared + mg-kv-margin();
   let file = file_size(dvb-iq2());
   let kinds = [dvr-wirespan-kind(2162688, 2162688, 553648128), dvr-wirespan-kind(dvb-mib(300), 2162688, 553648128), dvr-wirespan-kind(dvb-mib(100), 2162688, 553648128), dvr-wirespan-kind(0, 2162688, 553648128)];
   let said = print_str("  ask kinds " ++ kinds.str());
   dvr-ask-reason(empty, dvb-gib(1)) == "" && dvr-ask-reason(empty, derived) == "" && dvr-ask-reason(empty, file + mg-kv-margin()) == "ask-denied:wired-cap"
    && dvr-ask-reason(dvb-vm(128, 20, 4, 0), dvb-gib(10)) == "ask-denied:reserve" && dvr-ask-reason(dvb-vm(128, 110, 70, 0), dvb-gib(10)) == "ask-denied:wired-cap" && dvr-ask-reason([], dvb-gib(1)) == "ask-denied:memory-unreadable"
    && kinds == ["slice", "stack", "between", "slice"] && dvb-probe(m);
  }
  // the probe's kind on a REAL scripted stack-size delta (the IQ2XXS layer-0 gate stack, 553,648,128 B) is RECORDED and ends nothing: the window's one run reads a stage's reading by the rules that hold, and a
  // 'stack' delta passes them while the machine is quiet and the lease holds; the judge writes the kind and the delta to the env and answers ''
  def dvb-probe(m) {
   let quiet = dvb-vm(128, 100, 10, 1);
   let base = dvb-gib(4);
   let lease = dvb-gib(33);
   let stack = dvr-stack(m);
   let slice = dvr-slice(m);
   let env = dvr-env(dvb-iq2(), m, 1, 1, 64, 64, 0, 0);
   let k0 = record_set(env, "ws-slice", slice);
   let k1 = record_set(env, "ws-stack", stack);
   let logged = dvr-log-add(env, ["wirespan", slice, stack, 0, 0, [0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0]]);
   let why = dvr-judge-wirespan(env);
   dvr-abort-reason(quiet, base, lease, 0) == "" && dvr-wirespan-kind(stack, slice, stack) == "stack" && dvr-wirespan-kind(slice, slice, stack) == "slice" && why == "" && record_get(env, "ws-kind") == "stack" && record_get(env, "ws-delta") == stack;
  }

  // ---- 16: the holders ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  // a process row: pid ppid exe cwd argv start withheld
  def dvb-row(pid, exe, argv, start) = [pid, 1, exe, "/w", argv, start, 0];
  def dvb-holders() {
